PAUSE(2)                       P32W Unix                        PAUSE(2)

NAME
       pause - wait for a signal

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int pause(void);

DESCRIPTION
       pause suspends the calling process until a signal arrives
       that is not ignored. If the signal's action is to terminate
       the process, pause does not return; if it is caught, the
       handler runs and then pause returns.

RETURN VALUE
       -1, with errno EINTR, always.

SEE ALSO
       alarm(2), signal(2), kill(2), sleep(1)
